<div id="view-ops">
<div class="lead">Each AI operator is <b>a commercial or SiC semiconductor engineering workflow turned into an autonomous team of agents</b>. One track wins the work: it finds automotive EV OEMs, solar inverter manufacturers, and industrial power suppliers transitioning from silicon IGBTs to Silicon Carbide (SiC) MOSFETs, quotes 1200V bare die and power modules, responds to multi-year vehicle platform tenders, and tracks SiC market adoption. The other track delivers the semiconductor engineering and fab production: it runs AEC-Q101 automotive reliability audits at 175°C, optimizes 200mm (8-inch) Mohawk Valley SiC wafer fab yields, generates 1200V dynamic power test vectors, and manages SiC die mask ECOs. Point one at an EV OEM account, an 8-inch wafer probe map, or a dynamic double-pulse test file and it runs the loop, then hands back a review-ready output for a semiconductor lead to approve.</div>
<div class="legend">
<span><span class="tag commercial">Commercial</span> find, quote, tender, win</span>
<span><span class="tag operations">SiC &amp; ops</span> AEC-Q101 test, fab yield, 8-inch, ECO</span>
<span><span class="tag hero">Flagship</span> the deepest example run</span>
</div>
<div class="econ" id="econ"></div>
